# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# The kernels the per-kernel isolation matrix is measured on (issue #281).
#
# One record per line, fields separated by whitespace, `#` comments ignored.
# No field may contain a space, which is what lets both `collect.sh` (bash
# `read`) and `crates/xtask/src/kernel_matrix.rs` (`split_whitespace`) parse
# the same file without a parser.
#
#   1 id             the row's name; `rows/<id>.row` is its measurement
#   2 class          which release class of `docs/plan/02-phase-2-semantic-epochs.md:153`
#                    this row covers
#
# There is deliberately NO policy-variant record here. Every boot below runs the
# same bare initramfs with no distribution policy loaded, which is what makes
# each row a statement about a KERNEL. A record that varied an AppArmor sysctl
# would produce a row that looks like a distribution row and is not one -- the
# distribution row has to come from the distribution, which for this repository
# means the CI runner's own `--print-isolation` output. See the "these are
# kernel rows" section of docs/book/src/isolation-kernels.md for the
# cross-validation that settles it.
#   3 release        the `kernel.release` the booted kernel must report; a boot
#                    that reports anything else is a hard failure, never a row
#   4 url            where the .deb was fetched from on the collection date
#   5 deb_sha256     the .deb's identity. THIS, not the URL, is what a row is
#                    pinned to: distribution pools prune superseded kernels, so
#                    a dead URL is expected eventually and the remedy is another
#                    mirror serving these bytes -- not a re-measurement against
#                    whatever the pool holds now.
#   6 vmlinuz        the member of the .deb's data archive that is the kernel
#   7 vmlinuz_sha256 that member's identity, so an extraction bug cannot pass
#   8 append_extra   extra kernel command line, or `-` for none. The base line
#                    is in collect.sh and is identical for every row.
#
# Adding a kernel is this file plus a `KERNELS` entry in
# crates/xtask/src/kernel_matrix.rs (which says what the row is FOR) plus a
# collection run. All three, or the generator refuses to render.

